Localise pending_parent_checks to close()

The deferred-parent-check queue's lifetime is exactly one
Structure::close invocation, so it has no business sitting on
Structure as a field. Lift it to a local Vec<DeferredParentCheck> in
close() and thread it through drain_equalities, typing, and
impose_concrete_type as a &mut parameter alongside the existing
conflicts vec.

resolve_parent_checks now takes the queue by value (and &self) instead
of mem::taking it from a field. The DeferredParentCheck struct loses
its pub(super) since it is private to the module again.

pull_morphism_types in StructureCat creates its own local queue,
imposes via impose_concrete_type, and resolves immediately. That
shortcut is sound because pull_types_backward only runs after a full
Structure::close has drained pending_equalities, so no later equate
can fire to rescue a queued parent disagreement on src_st.
